Tcpdump is a powerful command-line packet capture and network monitoring tool. It is similar to TShark, but it is generally more lightweight and commonly used on Linux and Termux.

However, tcpdump is primarily a packet-capture tool, not a traffic-modification proxy.

### 1\. What tcpdump can do

| Function                     | Tcpdump |
| ---------------------------- | ------- |
| Capture packets              |         |
| Inspect packet headers       |         |
| Inspect some packet contents |         |
| Filter traffic               |         |
| Save packets to PCAP         |         |
| Modify captured packets      |         |
| Forward modified packets     |         |
| Perform MITM attacks         |         |

### 2\. Useful tcpdump commands for Termux

Check installation:

bash
tcpdump --version


List network interfaces:

bash
ip link


Capture packets:

bash
tcpdump -i any


Capture HTTP traffic:

bash
tcpdump -i any 'tcp port 80'


Capture DNS traffic:

bash
tcpdump -i any 'port 53'


Capture HTTPS traffic:

bash
tcpdump -i any 'tcp port 443'


Save packets into a PCAP file:

bash
tcpdump -i any -w capture.pcap


Read a PCAP file:

bash
tcpdump -r capture.pcap


### 3\. Comparison of your network tools

| Tool       | Capture | Analyse | Modify                   | Forward                  |
| ---------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------ |
| Tcpdump    | Yes     | Yes     | No                       | No                       |
| TShark     | Yes     | Yes     | No native editing        | No                       |
| Wireshark  | Yes     | Yes     | No native editing        | No                       |
| Ettercap   | Yes     | Yes     | Yes, with plugins        | Yes                      |
| Burp Suite | Yes     | Yes     | Yes                      | Yes                      |
| mitmproxy  | Yes     | Yes     | Yes                      | Yes                      |
| Bettercap  | Yes     | Yes     | Yes, depending on module | Yes                      |
| Scapy      | Yes     | Yes     | Yes                      | Yes, with custom scripts |

### 4\. My recommendation

For an authorized Termux network-testing environment, these tools complement one another:

* Tcpdump: Packet collection.

* TShark: Packet analysis.

* Wireshark: Visual packet inspection.

* Burp Suite: Web traffic interception and modification.

* mitmproxy: HTTP/HTTPS interception and modification.

* Ettercap: LAN interception testing.

* Scapy: Custom packet manipulation.

Remember: Capturing encrypted HTTPS packets does not automatically reveal their contents. Use authorized test devices and traffic.
